---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import springImg from '../../../assets/posts/grand-prismatic.jpg';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout title="Grand Prismatic Spring">
	<main>
		<nav><a href={base}>&larr; Home</a></nav>
		<h1>Grand Prismatic Spring</h1>
		<img class="post-image" src={springImg.src} alt="Aerial view of Grand Prismatic Spring, Yellowstone National Park" />
		<figcaption>Grand Prismatic Spring and Midway Geyser Basin, Yellowstone National Park. Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>
		<p>
			The largest hot spring in the United States, Grand Prismatic Spring owes its
			concentric bands of color to heat-loving microorganisms living at different
			temperatures across the pool. From the air, the pattern resembles an eye.
		</p>
		<p>
			Seen from far enough away, terrestrial features start to look like the view
			from orbit &mdash; see <a href={`${base}posts/earthrise/`}>Earthrise</a> for
			the inverse: Earth itself seen small and whole.
		</p>
		<p>
			And for a very different kind of natural spectacle rendered by human hands,
			see <a href={`${base}posts/great-wave/`}>The Great Wave off Kanagawa</a>.
		</p>
	</main>
</Layout>
